# Sprint 2 Review and Retrospective

## What was completed 
During Sprint 2 the team developed the working prototype. The main features include appointment booking, cancellation and rescheduling. The prototype allowed students to view available appointment slots and schedule clinic visits online. Basic functionality for clinic staff to manage appointments and admin to manage users was also included.

## What went well 
The overall development process allowed the team to transfer the earlier design content and the wireframes into a functional prototype. Implementing the main system features also helped demonstrate how the clinic appointment system would work in a real environment.

## What needs improvement  
Over time some features could be improved such as the user interface design and adding more advanced functionality for the clinic staff and administrators.

## Final outcome 
The project successfully produced a functional prototype of the clinic appointment system. It also demonstrated how digital appointment management can improve access to healthcare services for university students.
